# {{.Name}}

Requires Go 1.26.0 or newer.

## Run locally

```sh
go mod tidy
APPLICATION_ENVIRONMENT=develop go run . serve --config-dir ./config
```

Check the service:

```sh
curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/health
```

The response is `{"status":"ok"}`. Press Ctrl+C to stop.

## Configuration

Edit `config/app.yaml` for shared settings and `config/app.<environment>.yaml`
for environment-specific settings. Set `APPLICATION_ENVIRONMENT` to choose the
runtime environment; the default is `production`.

Use `--config-dir` to specify a different configuration directory. Override the
HTTP listen address with `{{envPrefix .Name}}_HTTP_ADDR`:

```sh
APPLICATION_ENVIRONMENT=develop {{envPrefix .Name}}_HTTP_ADDR=127.0.0.1:9090 go run . serve
```

## Build and run

```sh
go build -o bin/{{.Name}} .
APPLICATION_ENVIRONMENT=production ./bin/{{.Name}} serve --config-dir ./config
```
